**Calculation:**

1² = 1, 9² = 81 (unit digit = 1); 

2² = 4, 8² = 64 (unit digit = 4);

3² = 9, 7² = 49 (unit digit = 9);

4² = 16 (unit digit = 6), 6² = 36 (unit digit = 6);

5² = 25 (unit digit = 5)

∴ A perfect square number can never have the digit 3 at the unit’s place

